{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "updated_at": "2026-10-07",
  "notes": [
    "Provider-level catalog: WHO Jupiter can talk to and HOW credentials are organised (provider -> accounts -> credentials). It never contains a secret: every credential names environment variables, and values are read only from the process environment (.env / host secrets).",
    "Model capabilities are NOT declared here. They live per model in config/model_registry.json and are recorded only from real provider support after integration and verification. A planned provider therefore has no capabilities yet.",
    "Rate limits / free-tier ceilings live in config/quota_limits.json (provider and model sections). A free tier is never assumed permanent: free_tier.status is 'unverified' until a quota entry with a source exists.",
    "Google Gemini accounts and credentials are owned by config/credential_policy.py (priority order, per-credential model restrictions, project quota groups); this catalog only points there.",
    "To add another key for an integrated provider: add a credential (its own env NAME, e.g. GROQ_API_KEY_2) under an existing or new account. Lower priority numbers are tried first; a model row may pin one credential with credential_owner_id.",
    "kind: model_provider = serves models directly; gateway = one API in front of many upstream model providers; specialist_api = a non-chat service (search, OCR, speech, data, security, email); router = self-hosted routing software that forwards to other providers and is never itself an inference provider.",
    "free_policy is the DEFAULT free-only routing gate. Only 'recurring' providers with an integrated adapter serve automatic routing. Every other value (conditional_development, conditional_recurring, promotional_limited_time, signup_finite, paid, unverified, mixed, recurring_evaluation, recurring_development, recurring_noncommercial) is retained but excluded by default: unknown or conditional terms fail closed.",
    "Published allowances are planning data, not an account's remaining balance. Keys sharing a project/organization/IP never multiply quota."
  ],
